---
import Pic from '../components/Pic.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
import Assessment from '../components/Assessment.astro';
---
<Base title="The Decision Toolkit | Leadership Frameworks by Jack P. Flaherty"
  description="The Clear Confidence Assessment shows where your decision process breaks down before a crisis makes it obvious. About three minutes, results to your inbox."
  path="/decision-making-toolkit" image="/images/jack-p-flaherty-teaching-whiteboard.jpg">

  <section class="dark">
    <div class="wrap split rev top">
      <div>
        <h1>The Clear Confidence Assessment: find out where your decision process breaks</h1>
        <p class="lede" style="color:#E3D5BE">Drowning in data? Do decisions still feel like a guess? You do not need more information. You need a cleaner process.</p>
        <div class="what">
          <p><strong>What it is:</strong> a three-minute assessment of how your organization makes decisions with technology, built from the framework in The Decision Switch.</p>
          <p><strong>Why it exists:</strong> most leaders do not have a decision problem. They have a structure problem, and it shows up at the moment it costs the most.</p>
          <p><strong>What you get:</strong> your Clear Confidence Score from 0 to 100, the decision-making tier you are in, your single biggest gap named, and a personalized report sent to your inbox.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="btn" href={site.assessment} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Take the assessment</a>
      </div>
      <Pic src="jack-p-flaherty-teaching-whiteboard.jpg" alt="Jack P. Flaherty teaching at a whiteboard" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tight">
    <div class="wrap split top">
      <Pic src="jack-p-flaherty-workshop-table.jpg" alt="Jack P. Flaherty leading a workshop at a table" />
      <div>
        <h2>Most leaders do not have a decision problem. They have a structure problem.</h2>
        <p>After 25 years in risk and advisory, 15 of them at the Big Four, watching capable teams stall at the exact moment it counted, Jack built a method to move leaders from analysis to action without skipping the steps that protect them.</p>
        <p>This assessment is built from that framework. It takes about three minutes. It shows where your decision process breaks down before a crisis makes it obvious.</p>
        <p>It examines three areas every high-stakes choice depends on:</p>
        <ul class="checks">
          <li><b>Logic vs. Intuition:</b> Where are you over-analyzing, and where are you under-thinking?</li>
          <li><b>Risk &amp; Bias:</b> What are you missing that a more objective read would catch?</li>
          <li><b>Context &amp; Agility:</b> When pressure is real, do you move, or do you wait for certainty that never arrives?</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Your results go straight to your inbox, with a practical read on where your decision process is solid and where it needs reinforcement.</p>
        <p>Your decision process either works under pressure or it does not. This assessment tells you which.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What changes when your leaders decide faster?</h2>
      <div class="grid c3">
        <div class="card accent"><h3>Clarity</h3><p>See exactly where the "Certainty Trap" is stalling your progress and where your decision-making is already elite.</p></div>
        <div class="card accent"><h3>Momentum</h3><p>Get a personalized roadmap to bridge the gap between heavy data and sharp intuition so you can move faster.</p></div>
        <div class="card accent"><h3>Confidence</h3><p>Start leading from a place of absolute conviction, compelling others to follow, knowing you've identified risks others missed.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Assessment />

  <section class="tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="cta-band">
        <h2>Read the thinking behind the method</h2>
        <p>Short pieces on making decisions with technology, for health-system leaders, partners and the boards they answer to. Start with Fear Is Not A Control and Treat New Technology Like a New Hire.</p>
        <div class="btns" style="justify-content:center;margin-top:.4rem"><a class="btn" href="/insights">Go to Insights</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="dark">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="col">
        <h2>When decisions matter most</h2>
        <p class="kicker">When nobody saw it coming. When the information is incomplete. When the long-term impact is unclear. When the drivers underneath are not understood and the call gets made blind.</p>
        <p class="lede" style="color:#E3D5BE">Your team needs more than a strategy session. They need a framework they can run themselves.</p>
        <div class="btns"><a class="btn light" href={site.calendly} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book a discovery call</a></div>
        <p class="close">The cost of uninformed and delayed decisions compounds quickly.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 3.8vw, 2.9rem); }
  @media (min-width: 861px) { section.dark .split.rev { grid-template-columns: 1.1fr .9fr; } }
  .what p { margin-bottom: .7em; }
  .what { margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }
  .col { max-width: 40rem; }
  .col p, .col .lede { max-width: none; }
  .col .kicker { font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.45; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .col .btns { margin-top: 1.2rem; }
  .col .close { margin: 1.4rem 0 0; }
</style>

